Subject: [PATCH 2/4] test(claude-eval): G262-3 read-only compatible lock
 contract prototype

Not wired to core.persistence. Legacy mode: a read-only participant opens
the pre-existing canon lock O_RDONLY and flocks it, excluding the real
writer across processes and across a real read-only bind mount (where
'a+b' fails with EROFS). External mode: lock location and fingerprint
(dev, ino, ctime) resolved from a one-time manifest in the canon, so all
participants share one lock. Absent lock never created; substitution
refused, including inode reuse.

